---
title: Roasted Asparagus with Bulgar Wheat & Lentils
image: ./dinner/bulgar-wheat-asparagus.jpg
course: Dinner
tags: vegan
author: Jonathan Simmonds
servings: 1
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
---

Finely chop @red onion{1} in @sesame oil{2%tsp} and fry on a high heat in a #saucepan{}.

Once browned, add the @lentil verde{40%g} and @vegetable stock{300%ml}. Once boiling, turn down the heat and leave to simmer for ~{10%minutes}.

Meanwhile, chop @asparagus{80%g}, lightly coat in a little extra oil and place on a #baking sheet{} in a pre-heated 180°C oven (or air frier) for ~{10%minutes}.

Add the @bulgar wheat{60%g} and @lebanese spice{0.5%tsp} to the pan with the lentils and cook for a further ~{10%minutes}, adding a little more water if it starts to stick.

Prepare the dressing by mixing @tahini{10%g} with @garlic{1%clove}(crushed) and @boiling water{1%tbsp} until it reaches the same consistency.

Serve the bulgar wheat and lentils, applying the dressing and topping with the roast asparagus. Season with @black pepper{} and @chilli flakes{} as desired.

> The asparagus can be substituted for roughly twice the weight of broccoli or cauliflower. In this case, add a tablespoon of water to the oven / air frier to stop them drying out too much.
